      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nFixes engine startup for Pixtral (+ other models with the same problem) when a modality is embedding-only (`--limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"<modality>\": 0}'` with `--enable-mm-embeds`). This is the root cause of the failure observed in #65648.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Every model registered as of now obeys the contract that #32493 introduced.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n```shell\r\nvllm serve mistralai/Pixtral-12B-2409 --tokenizer-mode mistral \\\r\n    --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\": 0}' --enable-mm-embeds\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n#32493 added embedding input for disabled modality. It introduced the following split:\r\n\r\n- User inputs are checked against `--limit-mm-per-prompt` and `--enable-mm-embeds` once, in the renderer (`BaseRenderer` calling `info.parse_mm_data`).\r\n- Data the processor builds or re-parses is parsed with `validate=False`. #32493 switched both call sites:\r\n  - the dummy inputs used for profiling (`get_dummy_inputs`)\r\n  - the cache-miss items in `_get_cache_missing_items`\r\n\r\nThe split is needed because `MultiModalBudget` profiles each embedding-only modality with `mm_counts={modality: 1}` while its limit is 0. A dummy input that gets validated can never pass that check.\r\n\r\n4 models including Pixtral override `get_dummy_inputs` and call `self.info.parse_mm_data(dummy_mm_data)` with the default `validate=True`. This PR fixes the processor-side contract violation. Without it, any deployment of these models that relies on embedding-only modalities still crashes at startup, including KV/EC consumers that should receive embeddings.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\r\n",
